Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Every morning, before the city woke,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.01,0:00:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,my grandmother spread\Nfresh grass on the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.73,0:00:17.88,Default,,0,0,0,,She washed the green beans slowly.\NShe never rushed coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.88,0:00:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Then came the fire, and the smell\Nthat called the neighbours in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.49,0:00:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Incense filled the room.\NIt was her way of saying: welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.01,0:00:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The sound of grinding was\Nthe first music of my day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.20,0:00:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we waited. She taught me\Nthat waiting is part of the gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.33,0:00:55.93,Default,,0,0,0,,One pot. Many cups.\NNo one was ever left out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.33,0:01:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Three rounds: abol, tona,\Nand baraka, the blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.65,0:01:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,By the third cup,\Nstrangers had become family.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.65,0:01:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,'Stay a little longer,' she always\Nsaid. 'The coffee is still warm.'
